{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"The AWS review-bot holds a persistent tickets clone that a redeploy does not refresh, and it writes\non every Gerrit vote. Give it diverged-detection, and fix the deploy path so the change actually\nreaches the box. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why\nIts clone lives on an EBS-backed external volume (`docker-compose.yml:127`, `external: true`) cloned\nonce behind `if [ ! -d .git ]` (`Dockerfile.reviewbot:117`, itself nested inside\n`if [ -n \"${REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_PAT:-}\" ]` at `:112`), so a redeploy does **not** converge it. It\nwrites a `code_review` ticket and auto-pushes on **every** vote (`voter.py:260-343`,\n`REBAR_SYNC_PUSH: always`) — event-driven, not scheduled, so pausing AWS *schedules* does not stop it.\n\nThis is **new code, not a predicate fix**: `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` currently does only\n`git config user.email/user.name` (`:52-53`) then `run_ensures` (`:59`) — no fetch, no reset, no\nancestry test. Note its invocation at `Dockerfile.reviewbot:125` sits OUTSIDE the PAT block, so new\nlogic there runs even with the PAT unset.\n\n**Chicken-and-egg:** `autodeploy.sh:186`'s rsync — which is what refreshes the box's copy of these\nscripts — runs only when `BOT_PATHS`/`SECRETS_PATHS` changed (`:55` =\n`src/rebar/ infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot pyproject.toml infra/compose/docker-compose.yml`).\nA commit touching only these two scripts would never reach the box. So this must land in the **same\nchange** as an `src/rebar/` edit (A6-0a qualifies).\n\n## Approach\n1. Add diverged-detection to `reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh`: if `HEAD` is not an ancestor of\n   `origin/tickets` and not strictly ahead, `fetch && reset --hard origin/tickets`. Safe because\n   the bot never holds unpushed work (`REBAR_SYNC_PUSH: always`).\n2. Add `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` to `autodeploy.sh`'s `BOT_PATHS`, so future\n   edits to it deploy without waiting for an unrelated source change.\n3. After the combined A6-0a/A6-0b change merges, force or observe the review-bot deployment and\n   record a receipt tying the running container to the merged SHA or image digest.\n4. Before closing this ticket, execute an epoch-mismatch refusal probe inside the deployed\n   review-bot runtime and a diverged-clone convergence probe against its persistent tickets clone.\n   These direct observations replace any elapsed-time rollout proxy.\n\nVote safety\n\nVote safety is already guaranteed and must not regress: `voter.py:698` records the vote **before**\n`emit_code_review_artifact` (`:735`), and that call is wrapped in `except Exception` ->\n`_artifact_emit_error` + `logger.warning` + `return None` (`:368-371`) — documented as \"the vote is\nalready cast, so this never fails the review\". A store failure cannot wedge the `LLM-Review` gate.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Given a clone diverged from `origin/tickets` (no shared tip), the script\n      re-converges it to `origin/tickets` and leaves no local commits. Tier: **shell integration**\n      against two real temporary repositories.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Given an up-to-date or merely-behind clone, the script makes no destructive\n      change. Tier: **shell integration**.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] With `REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_PAT` unset, the new logic still executes outside\n      the PAT block. Tier: **shell integration**.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] `infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` appears in\n      `autodeploy.sh`'s `BOT_PATHS`.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A rebar store write failure inside the bot still leaves the vote cast.\n      Tier: **unit** on `emit_code_review_artifact` with an injected store failure.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The merged A6-0a/A6-0b SHA or image digest, successful deployment receipt,\n      deployed-runtime epoch-mismatch refusal output, and persistent-clone convergence result are\n      recorded on this ticket before closure.\n\n## Files\n`infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh`, `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh`, tests\n\nScope: S. Depends on A6-0a (and must ship in the same change as an `src/rebar/` edit)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785780376921507001,"uuid":"5b7fb3c1-36cb-4646-b146-77251391abe2"}